<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roberto Suazo Córdova</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a>–<a href="/years/2018">2018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roberto Suazo Córdova (1927–2018) was a Honduran country doctor and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> politician who was president from 1982 to 1986, the first elected under the constitution of 1982 after years of military rule. During his term Honduras became a base for US operations against Sandinista Nicaragua and received large amounts of aid, while real power lay with the armed forces under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavo-alvarez-martinez">Gustavo Álvarez Martínez</a> until 1984.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roberto-suazo-cordova.jpg" alt="Roberto Suazo Córdova" width="280" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: White House Television Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meeting_with_President_Cordova_of_Honduras_in_Rose_Garden_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
